						 <blockquote> <p>Also I am sure I have a green light. I got it by user DarknessAwaits.</p> </blockquote> <p><span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/darknessawaits" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2057158&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608453976" alt="DarknessAwaits" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2057158)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/darknessawaits" >DarknessAwaits</a></span> does not qualify to give greenlights, per the Ideas Critique forum required reading criteria.</p> <p>Also, reviewers will be very clear when they are giving a greenlight, often with <strong>bold text</strong> or <span style="color: green">colored text</span>. There is no mention of them giving a greenlight in their posts: <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13942203/book-of-the-undead">http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13942203/book-of-the-undead</a></p> 
